---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={"Privacy | Roos Instruments"}
  description={"Roos Instruments' Privacy Policy."}
  active={["nav-mobile-privacy","nav-company"]}>
    <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - START
    =========================== -->
    <section class="breadcrumb-wrapper">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <ol class="breadcrumb">
          <li><a href="/index.html">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/company.html">About Us</a></li>
          <li class="active">Privacy</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - END
    =========================== -->
    <section>
      <div id="content" class="container">
        <hr class="space">
        <div class="row">
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p>
            The privacy and protection of your personal and financial information is very important to us. This privacy
            statement fully describes our information gathering and dissemination practices. <strong>We will never sell
              any information gathered about you.</strong> Roos Instruments uses your personal information for building
            your Roos Instruments account, and facilitating the request for quote (RFQ) and RI Kit ordering process
            using the catalog and is fully compliant with the General Data Protection Regulation (
            <a href="https://gdpr.eu/">GDPR</a>) and California Consumer Privacy Act (<a
              href="https://oag.ca.gov/privacy/ccpa">CCPA</a>).
            Despite these assurances, please fill out the <a href="https://forms.gle/KRBgkAyeQVSWCFpLA">Do Not Sell My
              Personal Information</a> form to confirm your privacy preference. Send Requests to <a
              href="mailto:admin@roos.com">admin@roos.com</a>.
          </p>
          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            Roos Instruments only uses cookies while you are authenticated (signed on) for security and authentication
            and
            to facilitate searching with Google.
          </p>
          <h2>Use of Your Information</h2>
          <p>
            When you register with our site, we ask for your name, company name, phone number(s), e-mail address. Your
            initial password is sent to your email address, confirming your identity. We will use email or phone
            information to contact you when necessary. If you purchase a product or service from Roos Instruments, the
            information you give (such as your credit card number, purchase information, billing and shipping adddress
            information) is provided to the banking merchant. Details regarding the purchase are supplied to the
            international distributor or vendor partner when applicable. This is necessary to complete the transaction.
            We
            will not disclose your personal information to third parties, except to the extent necessary to provide you
            with a requested service, under circumstances required by law, or, in rare cases, to our business partners
            as
            outlined in this policy. We will never use your information for direct marketing purposes. You will not be
            contacted directly by any third party as a result of your relationship with Roos Instruments. Any business
            partners with whom we share your information will be subject to confidentiality restrictions preventing them
            from sharing your personal information with others. </p>

          <h2>Security Precautions</h2>
          <p>
            Our site has stringent security measures in place to protect the loss, misuse, and alteration of the
            information under our control. We use the industry standard SSL/TLS (secure socket layer) encryption and
            actively monitor and update systems used by the website. While we strive to protect your
            personal information, no data transmission over the Internet is guaranteed to be 100% secure. Thus, Roos
            Instruments cannot ensure or warrant the security of any information during transmission to or from our
            site, and you submit information to us at your own risk. However, we do our best to ensure the highest level
            of security on our systems. </p>
          <h2>Disclaimer</h2> (Full disclaimer is in the <a href="legal.html">Legal Notice</a>)
          <p class="text-justify">
            ROOS INSTRUMENTS, INC. SHALL NOT BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR DAMAGE OR LOSS OF ANY KIND DUE TO YOUR USE OF
            SOFTWARE AND/OR ANY OTHER PRODUCT OR SERVICE PURCHASED AT ROOS INSTRUMENTS. OUR MAXIMUM LIABILITY TO YOU IS
            THE AMOUNT YOU PAID FOR THE PRODUCT. WE DO NOT NECESSARILY ENDORSE PRODUCTS AND SERVICES MENTIONED AT ROOS
            INSTRUMENTS, INC. NEITHER DO WE MAKE ANY WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, ANY
            IMPLIED WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE), ABOUT THE PRODUCTS AND SERVICES
            IN
            OUR STORE OR THE ACCURACY OF OUR PRODUCT AND SERVICES LISTINGS. ROOS INSTRUMENTS, INC. DISCLAIMS ALL
            RESPONSIBILITY OR LIABILITY FOR ANY DAMAGES CAUSED BY VIRUSES CONTAINED AT OR WITHIN THE ROOS INSTRUMENTS'
            SITE OR WITHIN ANY ELECTRONIC FILES SENT FROM THE ROOS INSTRUMENTS' SITE. </p>
          <p>
            This site contains links to other sites. Roos Instruments is not responsible for the privacy practices or
            the
            content of these other Web sites.
          </p>
          <h2>Errors and Omissions</h2>
          <p>
            Roos Instruments works hard to ensure the accuracy of the product information in our online catalog.
            However, we are not responsible for typographical errors or technical inaccuracies.
          </p>

        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h2>General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) Specific Details</h2>
          <p>Roos Instruments intends to be fully compliant with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and will
            make the necessary accommodations for all of our customers, including those based in the European Union
            (EU), specifically by (1) getting explicit consent, (2) default data protection, (3) control of personal
            information sharing, transfer and disclosure, (4) rights of individuals, and (5) security. This document
            includes RI policy and information about partner tools used to respond to GDPR requests from EU residents.
            This also includes United States federal and California state privacy rules and regulations, where Roos
            Instruments is incorporated, that would also apply (i.e. reporting a security breach).</p>

          <h2>Privacy Policy and Explicit Consent Summary</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Requires that consent is given or there is a good reason to process or store personal information.</li>
            <li>Gives a person a right to know what information is held about them.</li>
            <li>Allows a person to request information about them is erased and that they are 'forgotten' - unless there
              is a reason not to do this— e.g. a loan account.</li>
            <li>Makes sure that personal information is properly protected. New systems must have protection designed
              into them (“Privacy by Design”). Access to data is strictly controlled and only given when required
              (“Privacy by Default”).</li>
            <li>If data is lost, stolen or is accessed without authority, the authorities must be notified and possibly
              the people whose data has been accessed may need to be notified also.</li>
            <li>Data cannot be used for anything other than the reason given at the time of collection.</li>
            <li>Data is securely deleted after it is no longer needed.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Assignments and Definitions</h2>
          Send Requests to <a href="mailto:admin@roos.com">admin@roos.com</a>
          <ul>
            <li>Data Protection Officer: Ryan Benech (rbenech@roos.com)</li>
            <li>Data Controller: Roos Instruments Employees & Contractors</li>
            <li>Data Processors: Roos Instruments, Rackspace, DuoCircle, Stripe, IBM, Google Cloud, Mailchimp, Dropbox,
              Microsoft 365,
              Apple iCloud, and possibly other services used by our Employees (i.e. Apps on personal or employer
              provided
              devices).
              Data Processing Addendum (DPA) links for all data processors are available by request.</li>
            <li>Data Subject: Individual identified or relates to Customer, Vendor, Prospect or any other category as
              appropriately
              assigned by business requirements or required by law.</li>
          </ul>


          <h2>Conditions for Collecting and Processing</h2>
          <p>
            Our standard website's <a href="legal.html">Terms and Conditions</a> and Privacy Policy (above) generally
            apply. Other information is collected and stored in the course of doing business (receive contact
            information,
            trade shows, etc...) and are used to conduct business. Examples of business practices include but are not
            limited to generating, storing and sending Quotes, Orders, Service Reports, Contact lists, letters,
            invoices,
            checks, deposits.</p>
          <p> Roos Instruments does not sell or share your personal information for any purpose other than described
            below.
          </p>
          <p> Uses of your personal data: For contacting in the course of normal business. We do not aggregate or
            analyze
            this information or share it with others.</p>

          <p>Opt-In Statement: You agree that Roos Instruments may collect, use and disclose your personal data which
            you
            have provided, for providing support and marketing material that you have agreed to receive, in accordance
            with our data protection policy (roos.com/privacy). You may change your preference any time by contacting
            admin@roos.com.</p>

          <h2>Rights of Individuals</h2>
          <p>We will accept requests for "right to know" or "right to be erased" by sending a message to admin@roos.com
            with the the requested identification information. "Privacy by Design" is implemented with our CRM
            environment
            and "Privacy by Default" means we will not share this information with partners unless required by law. Data
            is securely deleted when it is no longer needed (i.e. hard drives are destroyed instead of recycled.) and
            data
            retention policies are design to minimize exposure to breaches by providing access as needed. Employees can
            access information for performing normal business like responding to email and fulfilling requests for
            quotes,
            performing service, or other reasons.</p>
          <h2>Protection of Personal Information</h2>
          <p>Roos Instruments takes the security of your personal information very seriously. Roos Instruments online
            services such as the Website and internal customer relations management tools protect your personal
            information during transit using encryption such as Transport Layer Security (TLS). When your personal data
            is
            stored by Roos Instruments, we use computer systems with limited access housed in facilities using physical
            security measures. Personal data is stored in encrypted form including when we utilize third-party storage.
          </p>

          <h2>Privacy Policy Changes</h2>
          <p>
            Any changes to our privacy policy will be posted to this page.<br> Last Modified:&nbsp;Feburary 2022
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
</Base>
